(a) the objectives and salient features of the Prime Minister Research Chair (PMRC) scheme 2026 launched to attract accomplished Indian-origin researchers and scientists to Indian institutions;
(b) the number of Lead Institutions and Host Institutions identified so far under the scheme and the thematic areas of national priority covered;
(c) the number of applications received from Fellows and Host Institutions since opening of the portal, and the selection process being followed; and
(d) the financial outlay earmarked for the scheme and the manner in which it is expected to strengthen India's research and innovation ecosystem?

(a) the current status of Bharat Taxi, operated by Sahakar Taxi Cooperative Limited, including the number of registered drivers and customers, as on date;
(b) the cities in which the service is currently operational and the details of its proposed expansion to other cities, including the timeline for reaching 500 cities;
(c) the manner in which the driver-owned cooperative model is expected to ensure better earnings and welfare for drivers as compared to existing app-based ride-hailing platforms; and
(d) whether any regulatory or financial support has been extended by Government for the expansion of this initiative?

(a) the total quantity and value of cooperative exports facilitated by the National Cooperative Exports Limited (NCEL) since its establishment and the number of countries to which exports have been made;
(b) the commodity-wise break-up of exports undertaken through NCEL and the number of cooperative societies/farmers benefited thereunder;
(c) the steps taken to expand NCEL's export basket and market reach, particularly for value-added cooperative produce; and
(d) whether any price-realisation benefit has accrued to farmer-members of cooperatives as a result of exports routed through NCEL and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether any mechanism has been put in place to monitor if the micro food processing units that received assistance under the Pradhan Mantri Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises (PMFME) Scheme continue to remain operational after receiving assistance;
(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) the major reasons identified for assisted units becoming non-operational or failing to achieve the expected level of performance; and
(d) the corrective measures being taken to ensure their long-term viability?

(a) the current status of implementation of Production Linked Incentive (PLI) schemes applicable across various sectors;
(b) the details of investment received, production achieved and employment generated so far under these schemes;
(c) the details of the performance and top-performing sectors under the PLI framework, sector-wise;
(d) whether any mid-term amendments or extension of duration have been made in these schemes, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the details of the steps taken by Government to boost manufacturing, exports and the Aatmanirbhar Bharat initiative through these schemes?

(a) whether Government has approved the National Mission on Edible Oils–Oil Palm (NMEO–OP) with the objective of increasing oilseeds production in the country and achieving self-reliance in edible oils;
(b) if so, the details of the Mission, its objectives/targets,  timeline for its implementation and funds released to all States thereunder;
(c) the total budget allocated for NMEO–OP for the period from 2024-25 to 2030-31; and
(d) the additional steps taken/proposed to be taken by Government to promote indigenous oilseeds varieties, reduce dependence on imported hybrid seeds and make the country self-reliant in oilseeds production?

(a) whether Government is implementing the National Beekeeping and Honey Mission (NBHM);  
(b) if so, the  details and objectives thereof; and   
(c) the details of the steps taken/proposed to be taken by Government to increase honey production, scientific beekeeping and related advantages for agricultural productivity?

(a) the enforcement milestones of the Telecommunications Act, 2023, which replaces colonial-era laws to modernise the sector's regulatory framework;
(b) how the authorization-based regime streamlines administrative processes for providers and promotes innovation through the Regulatory Sandbox framework;
(c) the details of status of 2026 rules for principal, captive and miscellaneous services and Digital Bharat Nidhi's support for R&D, pilots and rural connectivity; and
(d) the specific measures under the Act to enhance user protection, such as mandatory consent for commercial messages and steps against cyber-financial fraud and spam?

(a) details of financial assistance extended to State Governments including Maharashtra and Gujarat for Modernisation of Police Forces with specific reference to advancements in weaponry, mobility and high-tech surveillance infrastructure during last three years;
(b) current status of implementation regarding Safe City Projects aimed at bolstering protection and safety of women within designated urban centres;
(c) status of deployment of Integrated Command and Control Centres and city-wide surveillance systems under Safe City Projects, the details thereof; and
(d) measures taken to strengthen emergency response systems and citizen-centric policing under Scheme for Modernisation of Police Forces and Safe City Projects including Maharashtra and Gujarat?

(a) the specific interventions implemented under the National Livestock Mission (NLM) to incentivise entrepreneurship in the poultry, small ruminant, porcine and animal feed sectors;
(b) the strategic framework adopted to mitigate the deficit in green fodder availability through the advancement of fodder seed production and pasture land restoration;
(c) whether specialised models for genetic breed-improvement and rural backyard entrepreneurship are being facilitated for landless and marginal livestock farmers;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the manner in which the livestock sector is being developed as a source of supplementary income and rural employment?

(a) status of guidelines notified following the Union Budget 2026-27 to accord Indian-origin status and import duty exemptions for fish harvested by domestic vessels within the Exclusive Economic Zone (EEZ) or High Seas;
(b) strategic framework adopted for the mother-child vessel model to facilitate mid-sea transshipment and augment the earnings of deep-sea fishing operations;
(c) whether digitised issuance of health and catch certificates via integrated portals has been operationalised to bolster product traceability and adherence to international standards;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the comprehensive initiatives implemented to enhance deep-sea harvesting potential while optimising price realisation and the global market competitiveness of Indian marine exports?

(a) the progress achieved under the "Sahakar se Samriddhi" vision in setting up new multipurpose Primary Agriculture Cooperative Credit Societies (PACS), dairy and fishery cooperative societies in previously unserved Gram Panchayats;
(b) whether the adoption of Model Bye-Laws has successfully empowered primary societies to expand their operational scope into diverse service-delivery domains;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the specific strategies formulated to bridge regional disparities and revitalise the cooperative movement in States where its presence is relatively low?

(a) whether Government has implemented the Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) system in the fertilizer sector across the country;
(b) if so, the details of its implementation and coverage, including the number of Point of Sale (PoS) devices deployed at fertilizer retail outlets;
(c) the manner in which the DBT system has helped in curbing diversion of subsidised fertilizers and ensuring their availability to genuine farmers; 
(d) whether Government proposes to further strengthen the digital fertilizer distribution ecosystem through technological interventions and real-time monitoring mechanisms; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of districts including Uttarakhand where the mandatory baseline study for identification of the ODOP product has not yet been completed by the State Government and the reasons for the delay;
(b) the number of micro food processing units formalised and supported under the scheme, including Andhra Pradesh and Telangana; and
(c) the branding and marketing support extended to promote ODOP products domestically and internationally?

(a) the number of farmers registered and claims settled under the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) during the year 2025-26;
(b) whether technology-based yield estimation (satellite/drone) has been adopted to reduce delays in the settlement of claims;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the details of the premium subsidy disbursed by the Centre, State-wise, including Uttar Pradesh?

(a) the progress made in finalising the Satellite Communication Network (SCN) Authorisation and spectrum assignment framework for satellite communication providers;
(b) the number of Non-Geostationary Satellite Orbit (NGSO) operators, including Starlink, Jio Satellite, OneWeb and Amazon Kuiper, awaiting licences or spectrum pending under this framework;
(c) the status and timeline in finalising spectrum pricing and security clearance norms; and
(d) the steps taken to align satellite broadband rollout with the National Broadband Mission 2.0 targets?

(a) the role of MY Bharat platform in mobilising and facilitating youth participation in the Prime Minister Internship Scheme (PMIS), in collaboration with the Ministry of Corporate Affairs;
(b) the number of youth who have registered for PMIS opportunities through MY Bharat platform, State/UT-wise;
(c) how many PMIS outreach camps and on-ground facilitation drives have been organised by MY Bharat across the country and what has been the participation in these camps; and
(d) how this collaboration advances the vision of a skilled and employable Bharat and the larger goal of Viksit Bharat @2047?

(a) the major initiatives taken by Government during the last two years to promote tourism in India, including infrastructure development and digital promotion;
(b) the progress and impact of the 'Ek Bharat Shreshtha Bharat' programme in promoting cultural tourism and people-to-people connections across States and Union Territories; and
(c) the steps taken to boost international tourist arrivals, ease of travel and development of specific tourism products like spiritual, eco, adventure and heritage tourism?

(a) the salient features, objectives and key components of the Kala Sanskriti Vikas Yojana (KSVY) for the year 2026-27;
(b) the details of financial assistance provided to artists, cultural organizations and performing arts groups under the scheme; and
(c) the steps taken to promote the creative economy, safeguarding cultural heritage and supporting emerging artists?

(a) whether the Land Port Management System (VINIMAY) has been operationalised at Integrated Check Posts (ICPs) across the country;
(b) the current status of integration of the system with stakeholder agencies;
(c) whether the Ministry has undertaken any assessment of the impact of the system on border management and trade facilitation, if so, the findings thereof;
(d) whether any roadmap has been prepared for expansion of the system to additional land ports; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the key initiatives undertaken by the Ministry for strengthening veterinary and animal healthcare services during Financial Year 2026–27;
(b) whether capacity-building programmes have been undertaken for veterinarians and para-veterinary professionals;
(c) the proposed coverage of veterinary institutions and personnel under these initiatives; and
(d) the details of planned financial outlay for strengthening veterinary infrastructure and services?

(a) the objectives and key components of the initiative for integrated development of 500 reservoirs and Amrit Sarovars announced in the Union Budget 2026–27;
(b) whether reservoirs and Amrit Sarovars have been identified for implementation of the initiative, if so, the criteria adopted therefor;
(c) the proposed coverage of Fish Farmer Producer Organisations (Fish FPOs), women-led groups and fisheries cooperatives under the initiative; and
(d) the planned investment, including the contribution of the Centre and the States, for implementation of the initiative?

(a) the details of fertilizer units that remained closed prior to 2014 and have been revived by Government thereafter, unit-wise; 
(b) the annual production capacity added through the revival of the Ramagundam, Gorakhpur, Sindri, Barauni and Talcher plants after 2014;
(c) the total investment made and employment generated through these revived units;
(d) whether any such closed units were revived during the period prior to 2014; and
(e) the reasons for which these units could not be revived earlier and the manner in which they have been made operational after 2014?

(a) the total production of Urea in the country during the period after 2014 as compared to the decade prior to 2014, year-wise;
(b) whether the country has moved significantly closer to self-sufficiency in urea production after 2014;
(c) the steps taken by Government since 2014 to augment indigenous production capacity of Urea; and
(d) the impact of these measures on reducing import dependence as compared to the pre- 2014 period?

(a) the details of Nutrient-Based Subsidy (NBS) rates fixed for phosphatic and potassic fertilizers during the last three years;
(b) whether Government has taken steps to keep fertilizer prices affordable for farmers despite volatility in international prices;
(c) if so, the details thereof and the additional subsidy provided to cushion farmers from price rise;
(d) the total subsidy released under the NBS Scheme during the said period, year-wise; and
(e) the measures taken to promote balanced use of fertilizers?

(a) the progress made in strengthening air cargo infrastructure under the National Logistics Policy and the Krishi UDAN Scheme during 2026;
(b) the airports and cargo terminals identified for expansion or upgradation, along with their current status;
(c) whether air cargo operations have been integrated with the National Logistics Portal and other trade facilitation systems, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to improve handling capacity and reduce turnaround time for export-oriented and perishable cargo?

(a) progress made in implementation of First Mile Connectivity (FMC) projects, including  number of projects commissioned, under implementation and proposed as on date;
(b) whether targets under the Coal Logistics Plan and Policy, 2030 have been achieved, particularly with regard to rail connectivity, mechanised coal handling and conveyor-based transportation;
(c) the bottlenecks identified in evacuation of coal from pitheads to end-use destinations, if so, the details thereof;
(d) measures taken to reduce coal logistics costs and improve evacuation efficiency through multimodal transport and dedicated rail infrastructure; and
(e) impact of these initiatives on coal dispatch and timely supply to the power plants and other consuming sectors?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to promote coal gasification and other cleaner coal technologies during 2026 including the State of Bihar;
(b) the number of coal gasification projects approved or under implementation, and their current status;
(c) whether any financial incentives or viability gap funding mechanisms have been introduced to support such projects, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the expected improvement in coal utilisation efficiency and reduction in emissions and enhancing domestic energy security through these technologies?

(a) number of workplaces across public and private sectors that have been onboarded on the SHe-Box portal, along with details of Internal Committees and Local Committees registered on the platform;
(b) details of measures undertaken to encourage adoption of portal across organisations in both organised and unorganised sectors;
(c) whether multilingual access and digital integration features have been incorporated to improve accessibility for women; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, including steps taken to strengthen compliance with the Sexual Harassment of Women at Workplace (Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal) Act, 2013?

(a) the current number of beneficiaries verified through the Facial Recognition System (FRS) under Anganwadi services for delivery of Take-Home Ration (THR), along with the extent of eKYC completion among eligible beneficiaries;
(b) the manner in which the FRS module has been integrated with the Poshan Tracker application for verification and service delivery;
(c) whether any operational or technical challenges have been reported by States and Union Territories including Rajasthan in implementing FRS-based authentication; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, along with measures undertaken to ensure accuracy, transparency and secure verification of beneficiaries?

(a) the number of villages, districts and States/UTs including Jharkhand covered under the Dharti Aaba Janjatiya Gram Utkarsh Abhiyan since its launch in October, 2024;
(b) the details of sector-wise interventions being implemented under the Abhiyan in areas such as infrastructure, health education, Anganwadi services and livelihood generation;
(c) the institutional framework adopted for coordination among the participating Ministries and departments for implementation of the Abhiyan;
(d) the details of financial outlay allocated under the programme, including the share of the Central and State Government; and
(e) the current progress achieved so far in bridging infrastructural and service delivery gaps in tribal-dominated villages under the initiative?

(a) whether the Directorate General of Training (DGT) successfully signed a Flexi-MoU with Bajaj Auto on 6th March, 2026, and other private companies for advanced manufacturing;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) how will the Industry-Integrated Skilling Model provide youth with hands-on training in high-tech automotive manufacturing;
(d) what specific role does the ‘Badhna Hai Toh Yahan Judna Hai’ campaign play in promoting these vocational courses; and
(e) how many youth have successfully enrolled in Aeronautics programmes at the new India-France Excellence Centre in Kanpur?

(a) the current status of implementation of the Centrally Sponsored Scheme for computerisation of Agriculture and Rural Development Banks (ARDBs), including number of units covered and States/UTs onboarded;
(b) the details of components undertaken under the scheme, including deployment of hardware, Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP)-solutions, digitisation of records and establishment of technical support systems;
(c) the financial assistance released by Government during the last three financial-years, along with the cost-sharing pattern between the Centre, States and ARDBs;
(d) whether the computerisation initiative has enabled standardised digital processes in areas such as loan processing, record management and financial reporting; and
(e) if so, the details thereof, including operational outcomes observed so far?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government has launched a Smart Agro-Textile Centre for the training and benefit of farmers with a view to promote the use of agro-textiles for agricultural development;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the list of products covered under the initiative, the cost involved in establishing such centre and the total number of such centres set up so far;
(c) the total number of farmers trained till date under this initiative; and
(d) the strategy adopted by the Ministry to extend the benefits of the programme to farmers across the country?

(a) the State-wise details of Rurban clusters approved under the Shyama Prasad Mukherji Rurban Mission (SPMRM), including Jharkhand, indicating Phase I and Phase II separately;
(b) the total number of gram panchayats and villages covered under these clusters;
(c) the criteria adopted for selection of clusters, particularly in aspirational districts and Left-Wing Extremism affected areas;
(d) whether any mid-term evaluation has been undertaken to assess if the selected clusters are economically viable and strategically located; and
(e) if so, the details of such evaluation?

(a) details of villages adopted under Sansad Adarsh ??Gram Yojana (SAGY) in phased manner since 2021, State-wise;
(b) total number of Gram Panchayats developed as model villages and the criteria used to assess ideal status;
(c) whether the Ministry has conducted any third-party evaluation of outcomes in terms of infrastructure, social indicators and livelihood generation;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) percentage of adopted villages that have achieved saturation in flagship schemes like PMAY-G, SBMG and Jal Jeevan Mission;
(f) whether any timeline has been fixed for achieving universal saturation of villages adopted under all flagship schemes of the Ministry; and
(g) if so, the timeline thereof?

(a) the manner in which the inclusion of ‘ergonomic berths’ and advanced noise-reduction technology has improved the overnight travel experience of passengers;
(b) the specific progress made towards the target of launching 30 new sleeper rakes by December 2026;
(c) whether the Ministry has successfully completed the testing of the 24-coach Vande Bharat Sleeper prototype at the Integral Coach Factory (ICF), Chennai;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the extent of reduction in travel time on the Howrah–Guwahati corridor as compared to conventional superfast express trains?

(a) the total number and value of projects sanctioned under the Agriculture Infrastructure Fund (AIF);
(b) the sector-wise and region-wise distribution of warehousing, cold storage, primary processing, particularly in Rajasthan;
(c) whether disbursement of sanctioned loans is proceeding as per schedule, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measurable outcomes shown by post-harvest loss indicators?

(a) how the ‘Living Roots’ festival has repositioned tribal music as a contemporary and economically viable force;
(b) what specific market linkages were established during the 14-day National Business Conclave for Tribal Entrepreneurs in 2026;
(c) whether the Ministry has successfully documented participating artists in the official Tribal Art Fest (TAF) Catalogue for international gallery exposure and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) how the Bharat Tribes Fest 2026 has successfully integrated over 1,000 artisans into the global value chain?

(a) the current status of implementation of the Scheme for Trans-disciplinary Research for India’s Developing Economy (STRIDE);
(b) whether the initial three-year cycle for the institutions selected under Component-1 has been completed and whether the evaluation reports have been received;
(c) if so, the details thereof including key findings in terms of research capacity enhancement, innovation and collaborative research outcomes;
(d) whether any expansion, restructuring or additional components have been included under STRIDE to further strengthen trans-disciplinary research in higher educational institutions; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the present status of implementation of Pradhan Mantri Uchchatar Shiksha Abhiyan (PM USHA), including number of States/UTs onboarded, units approved and funds sanctioned and released so far;
(b) the institutional and monitoring framework established at the Central and State levels for appraisal, evaluation and performance-based fund release;
(c) whether specific interventions have been approved for focus districts, underserved regions and New Model Degree Colleges; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, including expected impact on access, equity and quality indicators in higher education?

(a) the number of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) that have successfully migrated to the common Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP)-based national software as of March, 2026;
(b) the measures taken to provide broadband connectivity and hardware (biometric devices, printers) to PACS in remote and hilly areas to ensure that the digital divide is bridged;
(c) whether the National Cooperative Database (NCD) is now fully integrated with State-level Registrar of Cooperative Societies (RCS) portals through the newly released ‘Push APIs’ to ensure real-time data synchronization; and
(d) if so, the details of the integration thereof?

(a) the share of cooperative institutions in total agricultural credit disbursement over the last five years;
(b) whether stress-testing of cooperative banks has been undertaken in coordination with RBI and NABARD;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether a long-term recapitalisation or consolidation strategy for enhancement of the cooperative credit architecture is under consideration; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether all Fair Price Shops (FPS) have been equipped with electronic Point of Sale (ePoS) devices, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the present number of FPSs integrated with the Aadhaar-based authentication system, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government maintains a real-time dashboard for monitoring PDS transactions across the States, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government proposes to integrate the PDS database with other welfare schemes to ensure targeted delivery of benefits, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total value of India's chemical exports during the last five years;
(b) whether Government has identified major markets for expansion of exports of specialty chemicals, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the standardization measures taken to ensure global quality standards for chemical exports; and
(d) whether the Ministry has conducted trade negotiations to address regulatory barriers affecting Indian chemical exports, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current installed capacity of urea production in the country including Uttar Pradesh and the percentage of domestic demand met through domestic production;
(b) whether Government has undertaken modernisation or revival of closed fertilizer plants under the new urea policy, if so, the details of the same;
(c) the number of new fertilizer plants commissioned in the last five years in the country including Uttar Pradesh;
(d) whether Government proposes to encourage private investment in fertilizer manufacturing, if so, the details thereof; and 
(e) the steps taken to reduce India’s dependence on imported urea?

(a) whether the Ministry has integrated AYUSH facilities with the national digital health ecosystem under Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of AYUSH practitioners registered on digital health platforms and issuing digital health records;
(c) whether telemedicine services based on AYUSH systems have been operationalised in rural and remote areas, if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether the Ministry proposes to develop AI-based tools for AYUSH diagnosis, drug standardisation or treatment protocols, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the steps taken to create a national digital repository of classical AYUSH formulations and therapies?

